  "description": "Single day cell of a calendar grid (36x36). Renders a day number label over a colored/bordered background that communicates the day's state (default, other-month, disable, today, selected). TODO: radixPrimitive is a best guess — Radix has no native calendar/date-grid primitive; a day cell like this is typically composed as a plain <button role=\"gridcell\"|\"button\"> inside a hand-rolled or react-day-picker-driven Calendar grid, not wrapped in a Radix component.",
